.SH NAME
niac-attachment-policy-add - Approve an interface in the policy file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac attachment-policy add  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add one policy to the policy file, creating the file if needed. Run as root
(an elevated shell on Windows). Adding a policy the file already holds changes
nothing.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sudo niac attachment-policy add en16=direct
  sudo niac attachment-policy add eth0=access:200
  sudo niac attachment-policy add eth0=trunk:200,201,202
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-attachment-policy(1)\fP


